sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Acropora millepora Holocene Turing wavenumber at 385.2 µm (pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 82.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics (a=0.12, b=0.78, D_v/D_u=15.75) on a periodic 3.082 mm coenenchyme patch and solves D_u so that argmax σ(k) sits on the assigned 385.2 µm Holocene detail scale. The nonlinear FFT peak is 383.6 µm. A diffusivity sweep matches linear theory at Pearson r = 0.999986 (RMSE 4.06 µm). Equal diffusion is stable (σ_max = -0.038) and the activator standard deviation decays. The rendered GIF is the raw periodic field (dihedral 0) and scores cv_sim_similarity 86.1 against the Lundgren et al. 2013 colony photograph. The Murray band center is 319.4 µm and is not the target. The photograph is a colony, not a 385 µm micrograph. Overall 82.8/100 (faithfulness 80.7, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit dff4f2b508d0d1939f865c2f90f7ffe070e890d6; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0.py at dff4f2b508d0d1939f865c2f90f7ffe070e890d6, image/png, 1107243 B, 1568×1204 px, artifact_sha256 b961f6f44ace9b7168493e6db0302d044e9ed9b1fc77bc1a476480ed6ad43dac (sha256 b961f6f44ace9b7168493e6db0302d044e9ed9b1fc77bc1a476480ed6ad43dac), spec_fingerprint 9216d34e8500759b1989295cbfdfd4547358ffe09553264c746622fde6834013. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9216d34e8500759b1989295cbfdfd4547358ffe09553264c746622fde6834013; artifact_sha256: b961f6f44ace9b7168493e6db0302d044e9ed9b1fc77bc1a476480ed6ad43dac; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0/acropora_millepora_gbr_lundgren2013.jpg=94c2290198c33f39..., datasets/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=cf2e62d3f7797eca..., datasets/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=15285ac3d6dead24...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Dove et al. 2001: reef-coral colour patterns are GFP-like host proteins. | Lundgren et al. 2013: the CC BY 4.0 Great Barrier Reef colony photograph. | Wallace and Rosen 2006: Eocene Acropora skeletal diversity, out of this chronoseries.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u chosen so argmax σ(k) equals 2π/385.2 µm at diffusivity ratio 15.75. | Eight-wavelength periodic patch, seed 3104, explicit Euler. | Nonlinear FFT wavelength and the eight-point diffusivity sweep.; transfer_boundary: 385.2 µm is the assigned primordium-tier detail scale (log10 = -3.414), not a published caliper spacing of A. millepora pigment stripes. | The colony photograph is the computer-vision target. It does not resolve 385 µm.; does_not_claim: That 385.2 µm was measured on a micrograph of Acropora millepora. | That the spot field is a segmentation of the Lundgren colony. | That an in-series chronospecies predecessor or successor exists. The series length is 1, age 0 Ma. | That the Murray band-center wavelength (319.4 µm) is the selected mode.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add the discrete KS distance between those orientation histograms as a non-circular specimen metric.",
            "remediation needed: Draw the nonlinear ablation time series (activator standard deviation at D_v = D_u) on the comparison figure, beside the linear dispersion curve.",
            "remediation needed: Gauge-fix the eight dihedral copies of the periodic field and keep the copy whose 12-bin Sobel orientation is closest to the colony photograph." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.828"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

